  (label "LED_D3" (at 191.77 95.25 180) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid b1f827d1-c0c2-5812-81a1-bf82a06c0b8e))
  (label "LED_D2" (at 204.47 95.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 837a3c5f-1c84-5c17-802e-8492b9ed0d23))
  (text "TARGET NODE - one per target, up to 5, all identical (same firmware)" (at 15.24 15.24 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid 0d542f8f-9f3c-5484-ac2f-5d280adcfbb9))
  (text "As built: WeMos D1 Mini + battery shield (stacked) + SW-420 + one WS2812B. No wires to the hub: ESP-NOW radio." (at 15.24 19.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 50fb4a32-c06f-58a9-8b98-8a74acf41748))
  (text "BATTERY\nShield J2 closed: BAT+ -> 130k -> A0. The D1 Mini has its own 220k/100k divider on A0,\nso the ADC sees Vbat x 100/450 (1.0 V full scale = 4.5 V, ~4.4 mV per count).\nFirmware default batt_scale_uv = 4102 assumes 4.2 V full scale: calibrate each target\nonce in the app (Targets > target > Battery calibration) with a multimeter reading.\nSW1 (optional): with it off the cell is disconnected, so the shield cannot charge it." (at 15.24 63.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid ca142913-4748-5fca-8d0a-919dda9bc488))
  (text "Free pins: D0, D5, D6, D7, D8 (and D2 when JP1 is bridged to A).\nD4/GPIO2 = on-board LED and boot pin. TX/RX = USB serial console.\nThe 3V3 pin is the D1 Mini regulator output (feeds the SW-420)." (at 121.92 114.3 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 94073aa8-6b67-5a78-8b36-67eaf7182355))
  (text "HIT SENSOR\nPower from 3V3 so DO is 3.3 V logic. Rising edge = hit (interrupt on GPIO5).\nCoarse sensitivity: the module pot. Fine: lockout and pulses in the app." (at 190.5 55.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 1987d3ff-3220-5f6e-9dc0-ccddb6635b7e))
  (text "LED\nJP1 A = D3/GPIO0 (current targets). JP1 B = D2/GPIO4 (recommended for new\ntargets; set \"LED pin\" for that target in the app). GPIO0 is a boot pin: if the\nLED holds it low at power-up, the board starts in flash mode.\nWS2812B on 5 V with 3.3 V data is marginal (needs 0.7 x VDD) but works for one\nLED. If it flickers, power the LED from 3V3 instead.\nR1 330R and C1 100uF: recommended, not fitted on every target." (at 190.5 123.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid af6f4541-8117-52ea-ba53-d9a9555a6cd5))
